### NCBI

The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is one of the largest repositories of biological data. It provides access to 
nucleotide and protein sequences, gene information, genomes, scientific literature, and a variety of bioinformatics tools such as BLAST.
In this project, NCBI was used to retrieve the required biological sequences using accession numbers or gene/protein names, which were
then used for downstream analyses including sequence alignment, structure prediction, and phylogenetic studies.

